ab0","title":"Young armadillo (variant 4)","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/zone34%20zombie%20f","title":"Zombified warrior woman (variant 3)","variant":""}],"title":"Creatures and people"},{"id":"quest","rows":[{"detail":"","key":"quest/q13j","title":"A Map of the Region","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"quest/q14j","title":"Dangerous Neighbours","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"quest/q20j","title":"The Alliance","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"quest/q15j","title":"The Crossing","variant":""}],"title":"Quests"},{"id":"exit","rows":[{"detail":"","key":"map/gz33j","title":"Dar-Ulgorn fortress","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz34d1","title":"June cache","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz35j","title":"Sadrok and its surroundings","variant":""}],"title":"Connected locations"}],"versions":[{"guide":"","html":"<article><h1>Two Rivers</h1><p>Two rivers give this region its name. War reduced the city between them to ruins and turned its inhabitants into undead. The strategic position now holds a large Hadagan camp.</p><h2>The Joon cache and allies for the assault</h2><p>The sealed cache supplies Kir with Joon armour, but Tui-Len warns him against relying on hatred alone. He gives him an amulet that can turn dangerous creatures into allies. Rad identifies suitable hunting grounds for a cyclops and a dragon. Their recruitment changes the military balance and answers the baron’s objection that his soldiers cannot face Firez’s necromancy in a direct assault. Virril finally orders the attack. Before the confrontation, Rad speaks of the quiet home and family he hopes to have when his secret work is finished. The cache is found in the valley Rad hopes to settle after the war. Dartas’s account of a nearby village destroyed by harpies points Kir to the rectangular amulet needed at its sealed entrance; Tui-Len supplies the remaining magical help. During the assault, Firez sends the city’s population, transformed into undead, against the Canian force. Kir must break through this army to reach the palace. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]</p><p>Some story sections are unavailable because the installed sources differ from those used for this article.</p><h2>Sources</h2><p>Based on the original dialogue, quest journals, event scripts and world descriptions. Source numbers identify the evidence listed below.</p><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>#</th><th>Sources</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/junofil\">Tui-Len</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_343)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/doctor\">Uncle Rad</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_344)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/baron\">Baron Virril</a> (briefing brief_347)</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/doctor\">Uncle Rad</a> (briefing brief_348)</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/doctor\">Uncle Rad</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_330)</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/bson\">Dartas</a> (briefing brief_336)</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/junofil\">Tui-Len</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_341)</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Quest journal · The Citadel (quest q21j)</td></tr></table><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>Property</th><th>Value</th></tr><tr><td>Island</td><td><a href=\"wiki://allod/jigran\">Jigran</a></td></tr></table><h2>Connected locations</h2><table data-columns=\"1\"><tr><th>Maps</th></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://map/gz34d1\">June cache</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://map/gz33j\">Dar-Ulgorn fortress</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://map/gz35j\">Sadrok and its surroundings</a></td></tr></table><h2>Quests</h